WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.069
- Please welcome former
American Idol artist Casey

00:00:03.069 --> 00:00:07.179
and former artist from
The Voice Meagan McNeal.

00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:09.220
(crowd applauds, cheers)

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:10.250
I love this.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.260
It's like blending my two worlds.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.010
I love it; I'm so excited
to have you both on.

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:15.940
But each of you is doing something unique,

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:17.000
so Meagan we'll start with you.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.180
You were on The Voice like
right before I started,

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:20.013
- Yeah.
- right?

00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:20.846
- Yep. I was like,
- I just missed you.

00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:22.000
- Season 13.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.450
- Oh, that's the number today.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.283
- That's the number.

00:00:24.283 --> 00:00:25.116
- Yeah.

00:00:25.116 --> 00:00:27.690
- So, I think that's the
season that Chloe Kohanski won.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:29.470
And I'm from Chicago,

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.530
and so I landed on Jennifer Hudson's team,

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:32.363
which was like

00:00:32.363 --> 00:00:33.222
- Yes, I love her.

00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:35.970
I've always respected her.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:38.430
All right, well, we have a
video actually of Meagan singing

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:40.320
on Chicago's L train
recently that went viral.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:41.779
Take a look.

00:00:41.779 --> 00:00:43.328
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:43.328 --> 00:00:44.161
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:44.161 --> 00:00:45.745
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:47.968
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.227
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:50.227 --> 00:00:53.702
♪ I heard you say. ♪

00:00:53.702 --> 00:00:56.952
(upbeat trumpet music)

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.790
- Such a mama rocking that baby, what?

00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:07.407
I'm like, I mean, as a mom
who has rocked a baby before

00:01:07.407 --> 00:01:09.704
because like I never looked that cool.

00:01:09.704 --> 00:01:12.210
Like you have your baby
wrapped up while you're like

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.043
hitting those notes.

00:01:13.043 --> 00:01:16.160
That's some big notes
on a train, especially.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:19.570
- You know we, I was like
I, out of all the singing

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:22.469
that I've been doing, you know,
this video of us on a train

00:01:22.469 --> 00:01:24.563
just kind of like chillin', hanging out,

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:26.960
is the one that's gotten
all this attention.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:29.890
But I'm like, it is the
most authentic, like,

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.700
expression of myself, because I'm like,

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:33.208
I'm not taking the stroller on the train.

00:01:33.208 --> 00:01:36.270
So what happened is a
friend of mine, Avery Young,

00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:39.030
called me to be a part of this series,

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.440
the Floating Arts Museum.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:43.520
And Avery, he's like
there's always performers

00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:45.230
on the platforms in Chicago

00:01:45.230 --> 00:01:46.720
but we wanna like push the boundaries,

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:48.333
take it a step further, and like bring

00:01:48.333 --> 00:01:51.350
this musical experience to
people on the train car.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.830
And I was like, "Sign me up, I love it."

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.640
And he says, so, "We're
gonna do this series

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.410
called 'Soul L.' We're
gonna bring the performance

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:58.560
right on the train."

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.300
And I said, "Well I'm
free that day, Avery,

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.984
but I'm not getting a
sitter, so I'm bringing

00:02:03.984 --> 00:02:04.817
my little baby with me."

00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:05.890
And instead of like putting him

00:02:05.890 --> 00:02:06.930
in the stroller on the train,

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:09.180
I just put him in this MOBY Wrap,

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:10.013
and I said, "Come on Mason,

00:02:10.013 --> 00:02:11.120
- You look so cool.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:11.953
- Thanks.

00:02:11.953 --> 00:02:13.460
- I'm like, I would have
tried to do the same thing

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:14.970
and it would've not been that,

00:02:14.970 --> 00:02:16.736
- It would've been great.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:18.070
It would've been great.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:22.386
- But Mason, I sung with him
up until about 8 1/2 months

00:02:22.386 --> 00:02:24.730
being pregnant with him
so he's used to like,

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.650
all of the music and everything.

00:02:27.650 --> 00:02:29.880
- Didn't you find it hard,
though, there at the end?

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.630
Like your diaphragm just changes.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:32.610
Like the end of pregnancy,

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.685
- Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Not you?

00:02:33.685 --> 00:02:34.518
- No, no, no.

00:02:34.518 --> 00:02:35.541
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:35.541 --> 00:02:37.745
- I was like me either,
I've just read about it.

00:02:37.745 --> 00:02:39.990
I nailed everything.

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.550
- No, at the end of my preganancy,

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.710
people wanted me to record something

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:46.416
and I was like, ugh, like
I couldn't get breath.

00:02:46.416 --> 00:02:47.249
It was horrible.

00:02:47.249 --> 00:02:48.141
- It was pretty awful.

00:02:48.141 --> 00:02:48.974
- I know, I know.

00:02:48.974 --> 00:02:50.606
Well, what's the goal
behind these performances?

00:02:50.606 --> 00:02:54.650
- So the Floating Arts Museum
wants to connect people

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.743
through arts, culture, and music.

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:59.930
Just to do different programming
to push those boundaries

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:00.763
and to bring people together.

00:03:00.763 --> 00:03:01.596
- Yeah.

00:03:01.596 --> 00:03:03.390
- Which I was so grateful for
because that's the only thing

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.709
I ever want to use my
voice for is to regardless

00:03:05.709 --> 00:03:09.306
of class, race, gender, you know,

00:03:09.306 --> 00:03:10.139
- That's the thing about music.

00:03:10.139 --> 00:03:10.972
- to just bring

00:03:10.972 --> 00:03:12.355
- It brings everybody together.

00:03:12.355 --> 00:03:13.834
- It just is a language that, you know,

00:03:13.834 --> 00:03:15.055
that connects people.

00:03:15.055 --> 00:03:18.950
And, so for that to happen in that space

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.671
was just, you know, a dream.

00:03:20.671 --> 00:03:23.560
And it doesn't get more Chicago than like

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:26.620
deep house music on
the train in, you know,

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.453
- I think that's cool.

00:03:27.453 --> 00:03:29.424
I think that's gonna become
like a tourist attraction.

00:03:29.424 --> 00:03:30.257
- You know I think,

00:03:30.257 --> 00:03:31.186
- People are gonna go,
"Wait have you done this?"

00:03:31.186 --> 00:03:32.370
'cause I'd go.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:34.700
You were on Season 13,
right, with Jennifer Lopez?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.533
She was a judge?

00:03:35.533 --> 00:03:36.500
- Yes.
- Yeah.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.281
- And I do have to say she's
shockingly beautiful in person.

00:03:38.281 --> 00:03:39.114
- It's annoying.

00:03:39.114 --> 00:03:40.717
- Almost hard to look

